Subject: [PATCH] Abort on an exception escaping an event-loop callback

From guybedford/emscripten gbedford/callback-exception-abort, without its
test. callUserCallback handled any exception other than exit/unwind
through handleException, which rethrows it to the host (quit_) and leaves
the runtime running. From a timer, immediate or epoll listener delivery
there is no caller to receive it, and a JS exception (e.g. thrown by an
import) that unwound Rust frames leaves the program wedged: it now aborts
(abort(), Module.onAbort), as an uncaught panic does.

Base-commit: d6c521a7f (tag 6.0.10), after sourcemap-line-zero.patch

---
diff --git a/src/lib/libcore.js b/src/lib/libcore.js
--- a/src/lib/libcore.js
+++ b/src/lib/libcore.js
@@ -2175,9 +2175,13 @@ addToLibrary({
     try {
       return func();
     } catch (e) {
+      // No caller receives an exception from an event-loop callback, and one
+      // that unwound wasm frames leaves the program state undefined: like an
+      // uncaught exception in a native program, it is fatal.
+      if (!(e instanceof ExitStatus || e == 'unwind')) abort(e?.stack ?? e);
       handleException(e);
     } finally {
-      maybeExit();
+      if (!ABORT) maybeExit();
     }
   },
 
